      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To make this recipe easy to follow, I've broken it down into clear steps. \n\nFirst, season 4 boneless, skinless chicken thighs with salt and pepper. Heat a large pan with a couple of tablespoons of oil over medium-high heat. Sear the chicken thighs until they're nicely browned on both sides. Remove the chicken from the pan and set it aside.\n\nNext, reduce the heat to medium and add a minced clove of garlic and a diced onion to the pan. Cook until the onion is translucent, about 3-4 minutes. \n\nNow, pour in 1/2 cup of heavy cream and sprinkle 1/4 cup of grated Parmesan cheese into the pan. Stir until the cheese is melted and the sauce is smooth. \n\nFinally, return the chicken thighs to the pan and let the sauce simmer for 5-7 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through. Serve hot over cooked pasta of your choice.",
