      "content": "thanks for this. it looks pretty good and is definitely much clearer than the original. \n\ni ran it through our preliminary checker and the thoroughness score came back a bit lower than we usually aim for in the premium editions. i know you said you didn't want to keyword stuff, but i think we could probably add a bit more detail to the steps to help the score move up without making it feel totally ridiculous. \n\ncould you try another version? maybe go into more detail during the cooking process so the ingredient mentions feel more natural? just make sure it still reads like a professional recipe and doesn't just look like a list of words.",
