      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To make this recipe easy to follow, I've broken it down into clear steps. \n\nFirst, season 4 boneless, skinless chicken thighs with salt and pepper. Heat a large pan with a couple of tablespoons of oil over medium-high heat. Sear the chicken thighs until they're nicely browned on both sides, about 5-6 minutes per side. Remove the chicken from the pan and set it aside.\n\nNext, reduce the heat to medium and add a minced clove of garlic to the pan. Cook for 1 minute, until fragrant, then add a diced onion. Cook until the onion is translucent, about 3-4 minutes, stirring occasionally. \n\nNow, pour in 1/2 cup of heavy cream and sprinkle 1/4 cup of grated Parmesan cheese into the pan. Stir until the cheese is melted and the sauce is smooth, about 2-3 minutes. \n\nFinally, return the chicken thighs to the pan and let the sauce simmer for 5-7 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce has thickened slightly. Serve hot over cooked pasta of your choice.",
